{"seq":17,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:52:18.469Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"3ef7b312e3ec33111cca1776cff37f632a07005ace2f8d0a4f106c27e7da205b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Bettina Kroll, here's what I found for Kwame's review. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests/cheat sheet. There's very little, and the channels have no PHL or DMF tickets at all.\n\n*Pellucid Harbor Logistics (Gulf Coast)*\n• #4419: open. The `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n• PD-8841: chassis pool holds on double-booked gates, Gate 4B. Source: your 2025-12-08 Pellucid cutover recap, not Moss's notes. Included in case it's still live.\n\n*Driftmoor Marine Freight (Puget Sound)*\n• Feature request #882: bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers. Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.\n• #4419: the 2025-11-02 Moss digest ties this number to Driftmoor (barge slip 7 schedule sync, plus a patched manifest CSV before the 06:00 shift). See the flag below.\n• No ticket number is given for the Terminal B tide-table import macro failure. Engineering sent a manual CSV patch to the night dispatcher. Source: cheat sheet.\n\n*Flags*\n• #4419 is attributed to PHL in the cheat sheet and to the Driftmoor/Puget Sound account in the 11/2 digest. I can't tell which is right, so Kwame should confirm before it goes on either list.\n• I left out Pellow Home Living: PD-4821 and #8812, which are the Pellow door 6 and Door 4B tickets. I also left out the Saltmarsh tickets PD-4824 and PD-4827.\n• I can't see the account ticket folders under accounts/, so if there are other tickets for these two accounts, they aren't in this list.","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","thread_ts":"1791986400.000123"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:52:18.637Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"26ff4b96b4fb66764602df1de43338f56fbcdfedc5a671725dbb84e12ea02879","actor":null,"via":"runner","tool":"gbrain.ingest","kind":"admin","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124","author":"assistant","source":"team-coastal-members"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"fact_id":"2","source":"team-coastal-members","latency_ms":168,"status":"inserted"}}
{"seq":19,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-06-phl-tickets/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T23:52:23.837Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"1043a40b3b17072c32576ccddbf5a8f949976e7fc66172d2d79a54de4dbee344","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"I posted the list as a reply to Bettina's message in #coastal-team. There isn't much to list. I checked #coastal-team, #coastal-random and Moss's Coastal digests and cheat sheet, and the channels have no tickets for either account.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics**\n- **#4419:** open. The `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. This comes from Moss's cheat sheet.\n- **PD-8841:** chassis pool holds on double-booked gates at Gate 4B. This comes from Bettina's own 2025-12-08 cutover recap, not Moss's notes, so it may no longer be live.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight**\n- **Feature request #882:** a bulk-clear button for departed barges, requested by their warehouse managers.\n- **#4419:** Moss's 2025-11-02 digest ties this number to Driftmoor instead (barge slip 7 schedule sync). See the conflict below.\n- **Terminal B tide-table import failure:** no ticket number is given. Engineering sent a manual CSV patch.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Conflict on #4419:** the cheat sheet puts it on PHL and the 11/2 digest puts it on Driftmoor. I couldn't tell which is right, so I told Kwame to confirm before it goes on either list.\n- **Left out:** I excluded the Pellow Home Living tickets (PD-4821, #8812) and the Saltmarsh tickets (PD-4824, PD-4827).\n- **Not checked:** I couldn't see the account ticket folders under `accounts/`, so any tickets filed only there aren't in the list.\n\nNo finance figures were involved."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000125"}}
